# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Mente OS · .gitignore
#
# ⭐ IT LIVES INSIDE Mente/ ON PURPOSE — these are the tool's own boundaries.
#    Mente OS is a tool you drop into YOUR project. Everything it needs to
#    ignore is under this folder, so everything it declares lives here too.
#    A .gitignore written at your repo's root would be the tool reaching
#    outside itself, into a file that is yours — and you may already have one.
#    git reads every .gitignore in the tree and applies each to its own folder,
#    so yours and this one coexist without either overriding the other.
#
# ⭐ THE ONE RULE THAT DECIDES EVERY LINE BELOW:
#    a file travels if its content is true for EVERYONE.
#    a file is ignored if its content is true for ONE machine or ONE person.
#
# The engine travels. The instance stays. Anything carrying a name, a path, a
# repo or a measured number belongs to the instance and must not ship — a clone
# that inherits it starts up wearing somebody else's identity.
#
# ⭐ EVERYTHING MENTE OS WRITES LIVES UNDER THIS FOLDER — so this file reaches
#    all of it. The single exception is one line appended to YOUR CLAUDE.md at
#    the repo root: `@Mente/CLAUDE-MENTE-OS.md`. That import is how the router
#    gets loaded (a .gitignore never governs its parent, and neither does the
#    tool). That line is yours to keep or remove; nothing else of ours is up
#    there to ignore.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1 · GENERATED BY bin/init — never shipped, always regenerated ───────────
# These describe an INSTANCE, so they are produced on the machine that installs
# them, from templates/. Shipping them is the failure this file exists to stop:
# a clone arrives carrying the previous owner's name, and `bin/init` cannot fix
# it because it correctly refuses to overwrite a file that already exists.
#
# ⚠️ PROJECT-RULES.md is generated too, but CLAUDE-MENTE-OS.md is NOT: the
#    router is engine doctrine and ships identical to everyone. Only the
#    {{placeholders}} inside it get filled in on install.
mente.config.yml
PROJECT-RULES.md
docs/WORKSPACE.md


# ── 2 · SECRETS — never in git, under any name ──────────────────────────────
# A secret written here would land in every transcript that reads it, and a
# leaked secret is ROTATED, not deleted. Referenced, never pasted.
# ⚠️ The pattern is `secrets/*`, NOT `secrets/`: git does not descend into an
#    excluded DIRECTORY, so a later `!` negation inside it can never re-include
#    anything. Excluding the CONTENTS keeps the folder reachable for its README.
secrets/*
!secrets/README.md
.secrets-lease.json
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*


# ── 3 · THE INSTANCE'S CONTENT — the folder ships, what fills it does not ───
# ⭐ Read this block carefully: each folder keeps its README (which explains
#    what goes in it — engine doctrine) and drops everything else (the owner's
#    actual work — instance). The `!` negation after each rule is what lets the
#    empty folder travel with its explanation intact.

# the work — blocks and campaigns are this owner's open questions
work/blocks/*
!work/blocks/README.md
work/campaigns/*
!work/campaigns/README.md
!work/README.md

# live memory — where we left off and what is still pending are per-instance.
# ⚠️ principles/ is the exception INSIDE this folder: the owner-*.md files are
#    engine doctrine (the voice, the three architects), so they ship whole.
memory/*
!memory/README.md
!memory/principles/
# ⭐ AND THE SESSIONS FOLDER, for the same reason one layer down: its README is
# ENGINE doctrine — it names where the session history goes, so nobody has to
# decide it mid-close. 🔴 Measured 2026-09-09: nothing named that place, so at a
# real first close the assistant asked the owner where to keep the record, and
# their reasonable answer landed it in a path this file excludes.
# ⛔ The README ships; what an installation writes beside it does not, until
# `bin/init` adds the exception that versions its own history.
!memory/sessions/
memory/sessions/*
!memory/sessions/README.md

# the project's own thinking — architecture pillar and vision are per-project
Cerebro/*
!Cerebro/README.md
!Cerebro/vision/
Cerebro/vision/*
!Cerebro/vision/README.md

# connection/ — the outward door. Only the READMEs are engine doctrine and ship; everything
# else is INSTANCE: which other trees exist is a fact about ONE machine, and third-party code
# (skills/ mcp/ tools/) is never versioned — `bin/connection sync` restores it from the
# lockfile. The lockfile itself (registry.tsv) is instance data, versioned with `git add -f`.
connection/*
!connection/README.md
!connection/bridges/
connection/bridges/*
!connection/bridges/README.md
!connection/skills/
connection/skills/*
!connection/skills/README.md
!connection/mcp/
connection/mcp/*
!connection/mcp/README.md
!connection/tools/
connection/tools/*
!connection/tools/README.md
# cli/ · the README ships; a CARD per CLI is this installation's (`bin/init` versions them)
!connection/cli/
connection/cli/*
!connection/cli/README.md
# the heartbeat's CODE is engine; target.conf and state/ are one machine's facts
!connection/server/
connection/server/*
!connection/server/README.md
!connection/server/server
!connection/server/remote-health.sh
# named although connection/server/* covers them: declared, not inferred
connection/server/target.conf
connection/server/state/
# ⭐ named on its own line although connection/* already covers it: the frontier is
#    declared, not inferred — the lockfile is instance data and never ships from the engine
connection/registry.tsv

# which account governs which repo — real org and repo names live here
accounts.tsv


# ── 4 · docs/ IS MIXED — engine contracts ship, measured numbers do not ─────
# A number copied into a document is correct exactly once. These are rebuilt by
# bin/generate-index and bin/generate-metrics, so a committed copy would be a
# stale claim that still looks authoritative.
docs/INDEX.md
docs/STATES.md
docs/METRICS.md
docs/DECISIONS.md
docs/PENDING-*.md


# ── 5 · RUNTIME STATE — written by the engine while it runs ─────────────────
# Per-machine by definition. Committing any of these makes a clone "remember"
# something that happened on somebody else's computer.
# ⛔ git has NO end-of-line comments in a pattern: everything after the path is
#    read as part of the filename. Comments go on their own line, above.
cache/*
!cache/README.md
# the battery takes a lock; a committed one would block every clone
.test-lock/
# proof the session hook still fires — dated, per-machine
.heartbeat
# same, one per gate
.beats/


# ── 6 · PERSONAL SCRATCH ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Nota.txt
*.local
*.draft.md


# ── 7 · TOOLING NOISE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
